    <meta property="og:description" content="Immune cells are shaped by the tissue environment, yet the states of healthy human T cells are mainly studied in the blood. Here, the authors perform single cell RNA-seq of T cells from tissues and blood of healthy donors and show its utility as a reference map for comparison of human T cell states in disease."/>
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-12464-3/MediaObjects/41467_2019_12464_Fig1_HTML.png"/>
    






</head>
